course: dictionary
lesson: 5744
title: A word from Ireland: lough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one place. Lough is one of them. You will see it in place names such as Lough Neagh, and it means a lake, or a long, narrow arm of the sea, in Ireland. «Lough Neagh in Northern Ireland is the largest lake in the UK by area.» The sentence calls Lough Neagh a lake, so a lough is a kind of lake.
explain: Read the clues around the word. The sentence says Lough Neagh is «the largest lake» in the UK, so the clues point to a big body of water. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «lake» fits, your meaning is right.
explain: Scotland has a close cousin, the loch. «Loch Ness in Scotland, long, narrow and over 200 metres deep, holds more water than all the lakes of England and Wales together.» Loch and lough are both water words, but a dictionary tells you where each one belongs.
fact: A lough is a lake, or a long, narrow arm of the sea, in Ireland.
fact: «Lough» is a word from Ireland, and you will see it at the start of many place names.
fact: «Lough Neagh» is the largest lake in the UK by area.
fact: «Loch Ness» is in Scotland, and it is long, narrow and over 200 metres deep.
fact: A loch is the Scottish word for a lake, like a lough in Ireland.
exercise: «Lough Neagh in Northern Ireland is the largest lake in the UK by area.» What is a lough? | *A lake in Ireland | A hill in Scotland | A kind of sea bird | A type of bread
exercise: Where is the word lough mainly used? | Egypt | Spain | Australia | *Ireland
exercise: Which Scottish word means much the same as lough? | Lot | *Loch | Lore | Lock
test: «Loch Ness in Scotland, long, narrow and over 200 metres deep, holds more water than all the lakes of England and Wales together.» What do the words long, narrow and deep tell you about Loch Ness? | It is a mountain | It is dry | It is a city | *It is long, narrow and deep, so it holds a lot of water
test: What does the word lough mean? | *A lake or a long, narrow arm of the sea in Ireland | A river in Wales | A type of boat | A large mountain
exam: What is the best way to work out the meaning of lough in «Lough Neagh in Northern Ireland is the largest lake in the UK by area»? | Ask for a new word | Guess that it is a cake | Skip it and never come back | *Read the words around it and check that lake fits
